 :context
 "Live kotoba-lang/industry registry re-verified fresh before work began: :name
  'Publishing of directories and mailing lists' confirmed for {:id \"5812\"}
  (:maturity :spec, stale placeholder :repo/:business-id
  gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-J5812 predating the current cloud-itonami-isic-<id>
  naming convention). No prior cloud-itonami-isic-5812 repo existed (gh api
  404, confirmed before this work began). Built from cloud-itonami-isic-873
  (residential care activities for the elderly and disabled) as the
  module-structure template -- closest architectural sibling: same
  coordination-only shape, same closed op-allowlist pattern, same
  record-verification/effect-propose/scope-exclusion gate structure. ISIC
  5812 covers publishing of directories (telephone/business/trade
  directories, compilations of facts) and mailing lists (subscriber/address
  lists). This activity directly touches personal-data handling and
  privacy/consent decisions -- directory entries and mailing-list records
  routinely contain PII, and publishers are frequently the subject of
  opt-out/deletion/accuracy-dispute requests. Per the Wave-4 person-facing-
  service safety guardrail (ADR-2607152500), the closed op allowlist NEVER
  includes an op that directly finalizes a data-privacy-compliance decision
  -- those are always either a hard permanent block or an always-escalate
  op, never auto-commit-eligible; any 'flag a concern' op always escalates
  and is never in any phase's :auto set."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["directly finalizing a data-privacy-compliance decision (deciding a
   listing/subscriber record is GDPR/CCPA/opt-out compliant) -- permanently
   blocked, no override"
  "resolving or granting a data-subject deletion/erasure/'right to be
   forgotten' request -- permanently blocked, no override"
  "any other privacy-authority determination (consent adjudication,
   regulatory compliance ruling) -- permanently blocked, no override"
  "coverage beyond the seeded English/Japanese GDPR/CCPA/right-to-be-
   forgotten/DSAR terminology in the scope-exclusion term list -- a starting
   catalog, not an exhaustive survey of every jurisdiction's data-protection
   vocabulary"]

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-5812 with Advisor/Governor/Phase/Store/
  Operation/Sim (mirrors cloud-itonami-isic-873 module-for-module, adapted
  from residential-care coordination to directory/mailing-list-publishing
  coordination -- dirmailops.* namespace, DirMail Governor):
  - Governor: three HARD checks, all permanent and un-overridable --
    listing/subscriber record must exist AND be independently
    :registered?/:verified? in the store before ANY proposal for it may
    commit or even escalate (re-derived from the record's own store state,
    never proposal self-report); :effect must always be :propose; scope
    exclusion (folded together with the closed-op-allowlist check) blocks
    any proposal, regardless of op, whose text touches directly finalizing
    a data-privacy-compliance decision. One SOFT escalation gate: low
    confidence OR the op is :flag-privacy-concern (ALWAYS escalates,
    regardless of confidence).
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate, :flag-privacy-concern permanently absent from
    every phase's :auto set (structural, not a milestone) -- independently
    verified by a dedicated test
    (flag-privacy-concern-never-in-any-auto-set); :log-listing-record,
    :schedule-publication-operation, and :coordinate-distribution ARE
    auto-eligible at phase 3.
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore (default), String-keyed listing
    directory, append-only ledger + publication-log, 3 seeded demo listings
    (2 registered+verified, 1 registered-but-unverified to exercise the
    HARD-hold path).
  - Advisor: mock-advisor (deterministic, default), same proposal-EDN
    contract as every sibling actor; a dedicated test
    (no-proposal-ever-drafts-a-privacy-compliance-decision) asserts no
    default-path proposal text ever claims to finalize a privacy-compliance
    decision.
  - Operation: full langgraph-clj StateGraph (advise -> govern -> decide ->
    commit|hold|request-approval), real interrupt-before/resume approval
    workflow.
  - Sim: demo runner (-main) exercising the full happy path plus HARD-hold
    scenarios directly.
  - Ops (closed allowlist, all :effect :propose): log-listing-record
    (directory-entry/subscriber-list data logging),
    schedule-publication-operation (compilation/update/print-run scheduling
    proposal), coordinate-distribution (outbound directory/list
    distribution coordination), flag-privacy-concern (data-consent/opt-out/
    accuracy concern -- ALWAYS escalates). None of these four ops directly
    finalizes a data-privacy-compliance decision, satisfying the Wave-4
    guardrail by construction.
  - Tests: 43 tests / 132 assertions across
    advisor/governor/governor-contract/phase/store-contract, all green.
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop), AGPL-3.0-or-later.
  - GitHub repo created directly as cloud-itonami-isic-5812 (no rename
    fallback needed)."

